<article class="env-example" id="06BR">
<p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/06BR">Example <span data-tag="06BR">7.6.6.37</span>.</a> Let $\mathbb {K}$ be a collection of simplicial sets and let $U: \operatorname{\mathcal{E}}\rightarrow \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$ be a cocartesian fibration of $\infty $-categories. Then $U$ is $\mathbb {K}$-cocomplete if and only if it satisfies the following condition: </p>
<p><dl>
<dt>$(\ast )$</dt>
<dd><p>
For $K \in \mathbb {K}$, every lifting problem 
</p>
<div class="equation">
  \[  \xymatrix@R =50pt@C=50pt{ K \ar [d] \ar [r] &amp;  \operatorname{\mathcal{E}}\ar [d]^{U} \\ K^{\triangleright } \ar@ {--&gt;}[ur]^{ \overline{q} } \ar [r] &amp;  \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}} \]
</div>
<p>
 admits a solution where $\overline{q}$ is a $U$-colimit diagram in the $\infty $-category $\operatorname{\mathcal{E}}$. 
</p>
</dd>
</dl></p>
<p> By virtue of Example <a data-tag="06BL" href="/tag/06BL">7.6.6.32</a>, this is a reformulation of Proposition <a data-tag="06B2" href="/tag/06B2">7.3.9.1</a>. </p>
</article>
